    "body": "Dear Author,\n\nHello\uff01Thank you for the detailed work on Squidiff. I was reviewing the description of the training tasks and have a question about the iPSC differentiation prediction task.\n\nThe description states: \"we selected the top 203 most variable genes, balancing biological significance with computational efficiency.\"\n\nCould you please elaborate on the following points?\n\n1. **\u200bSpecific Number 203**:\u200b\u200b What was the rationale behind selecting exactly \u200b203\u200b genes?\n2. **\u200bSelection Strategy**:\u200b\u200b You mention balancing biological significance with computational efficiency. Could you detail the \u200bexact criteria and steps\u200b used for selecting these top variable genes\n3. \u200b**Model Requirement on Gene Count**:\u200b\u200b I noticed that other tasks mentioned  also seem to use around 200 genes. Does the Squidiff model architecture or training framework have a \u200bspecific requirement or strong preference for an input gene number in this range\u200b? \n\nUnderstanding the reasoning behind these design choices would be very helpful for applying and interpreting the model.\n\nThank you for your time and clarification.",
